From bc6542260ddfb04c4b6cd1b2c174ab18c4511590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uzair Akbar <uzairakbar025@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 04:35:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] fix(sim): scope visual lookups by model; fix
 double-prefixed link names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Visual snapshot cache and the command-apply link maps were keyed by bare
link name, colliding when models share link names (racecar vs bot_car) —
blink, car color and randomizer ops could land on the wrong car. Key
visuals as model::link::visual, share one dual-keyed link-entity map,
and let GetVisualNames accept scoped, bare or double-prefixed requests
while returning scoped names. Also fix blink_effect and
model_visual_randomizer double-prefixing already-scoped body_names,
which silently matched zero visuals.
